417] [17592186082512 #edb/ref 1080 "2x - 6 - \\frac{5}{x - 3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082512 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082512 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8742700c-068c-5112-9840-e1e8b69f8d04" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082513 #edb/ref 1080 "2x + 3 + \\frac{5}{x - 3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082513 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082513 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "911f86a7-0f0d-5c28-ae97-e43dfbb7d72a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082514 #edb/ref 1080 "2x + 1 + \\frac{5}{x - 3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082514 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082514 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "12768b59-45df-5645-92c4-6c584cb8c6a9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082515 #edb/ref 1080 "2x + 6 + \\frac{5}{x - 3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082515 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082515 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7194ebcd-7918-5ad3-ac00-2ef683e6bb42" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082516 #edb/ref 1080 "2x + 5 + \\frac{5}{x - 3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082516 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082516 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "738ace65-7d04-54a5-877c-589818b5b693" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083004 #edb/ref 1069 "e-5146" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083004 #edb/ref 1071 "Use synthetic division to divide $5x^4+x^3+6x+2$ by $x+1$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083004 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "551cceca-a69f-57c1-b4b0-c8f7aedd3cdc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083004 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that the dividend is missing an $x^2$ term, so we insert a $0x^2$ in its place and carry out the process in the same way.\n\n$$\n-1\\begin{vmatrix}5 & 1 & 0 & 6\\end{vmatrix}2; - 5\\begin{vmatrix}4 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 5 & -4 & 4\\end{vmatrix}2 \\mid 0\n$$\n\nSince the remainder is $0$, it means that $x+1$ divides $5x^4+x^3+6x+2$ exactly and gives a quotient of $5x^3-4x^2+4x+2$.\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{5x^4+x^3+6x+2}{x+1} = 5x^3-4x^2+4x+2\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083005 #edb/ref 1069 "e-5149" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083005 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the quotient and remainder of $\\dfrac{3x^4+7x^3-10x+8}{2-3x}$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083005 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6d179766-30a7-5cd9-ba38-2ee6f49d37b8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083005 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we write the divisor in standard form as $-3x+2$. Then, we factor out the leading coefficient. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{3x^{4} + 7x^{3} - 10x + 8}{-3x + 2} &= (3x^{4} + 7x^{3} - 10x + 8)/(-3(x - \\frac{2}{3})) \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{3}((3x^{4} + 7x^{3} - 10x + 8)/((x - \\frac{2}{3})))\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCarrying out the synthetic division process on\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3x^4+7x^3-10x+8}{\\left(x-\\frac23\\right)}\n$$\n\nremembering to include a coefficient of zero for the $x^2$ term, we arrive at the following:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{3}\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 7 & 0 & -10\\end{vmatrix}8; 2\\begin{vmatrix}6 & 4 & -4 \\\\ 3 & 9 & 6\\end{vmatrix}- 6 \\mid 4\n$$\n\nReading off the bottom row, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{3x^4+7x^3-10x+8}{\\left(x-\\frac23\\right)} = 3x^3+9x^2+6x-6+\\frac{4}{\\left(x-\\frac23\\right)}\n$$\n\nFinally, we multiply by the original\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac 1 3\n$$\n\nfactor to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{3x^{4} + 7x^{3} - 10x + 8}{2 - 3x} &= -\\frac{1}{3}(3x^{3} + 9x^{2} + 6x - 6 + (4)/((x - \\frac{2}{3}))) \\\\\n&=-x^{3} - 3x^{2} - 2x + 2 + \\frac{4}{2 - 3x}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083203 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049538 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083203 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186083822 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083203 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186083930 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083203 #edb/ref 1039 "Dividing a Polynomial by a Linear Binomial Using Synthetic Division" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083203 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186083004 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083203 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "c47216a0-3e51-50bb-b7eb-f92592db5dbc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083204 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186051079 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083204 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186083596 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083204 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186083597 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083204 #edb/ref 1039 "Dividing a Polynomial by a Linear Binomial With Leading Coefficients" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083204 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186083005 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083204 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "2b0a87cd-e9b5-5ca1-8132-b62a715264ac" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083423 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186084088 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083423 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186084089 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083423 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186084090 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083423 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186084091 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083423 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186084198 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083423 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186084273 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083423 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083423 #edb/ref 1045 "Dividing Polynomials Using Synthetic Division" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083423 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186084198 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083423 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186051061 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083423 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "bb6800d8-7ba1-553c-9322-ca9069cbaa8a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083597 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186080667 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083597 #edb/ref 1069 "q-19186" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083597 #edb/ref 1071 "What is $\\frac{18x^{2} + 27x}{6x - 1}$?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083597 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c2b65857-f961-5afd-9ef2-0421d5a69f7a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083822 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186081863 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083822 #edb/ref 1069 "q-5902" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083822 #edb/ref 1071 "What is $\\frac{4x^{3} + 2x^{2} - x + 1}{x - 5}$?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083822 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "de8f069f-9a0c-5798-9f23-be0540a99a8e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083930 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186082511 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083930 #edb/ref 1069 "q-7670" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083930 #edb/ref 1071 "What is $\\frac{2x^{2} - 3x - 4}{x - 3}$?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083930 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4aae2ef4-175a-54ac-96cd-b00f03406c30" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084088 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186084273 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084088 #edb/ref 1061 18899 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084088 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7e09c9d5-51c1-52a9-a8a2-2acf0b38cd4d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084088 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186084439 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084089 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186084090 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084089 #edb/ref 1061 18901 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084089 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7b4de1ae-1152-53f5-a47b-143b708404f8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084089 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186083203 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084090 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186084091 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084090 #edb/ref 1061 18903 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084090 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "270d71b2-4b1a-5d4d-a08f-5d2e45600ae7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084090 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186084440 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084091 #edb/ref 1061 18905 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084091 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "300c079c-b57a-5be9-a005-dc19f97ed3d8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084091 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186083204 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084198 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186084088 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084198 #edb/ref 1061 23194 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084198 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c1e715a2-551a-5990-b6c4-823e40d008ec" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084198 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186084466 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084273 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186084089 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084273 #edb/ref 1061 31046 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084273 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "cb6d802c-b294-5078-a70b-ca55476b9f22" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084273 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186084483 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084439 #edb/ref 1064 "Our goal is to find the quotient and remainder of the following division problem.\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2x^3-5x^2-7x+11}{x-3}\n$$\n\nTo do this, we can use **synthetic division**. Synthetic division allows us to divide a polynomial by a factor of the form $(x-c)$. Here's how we do it.\n\n| $3\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -5 & -7\\end{vmatrix}11$ | Start off by writing the term $c$ of the divisor on the left side. Here, $c = {\\color{blue}{3}}$. Then, write the coefficients of all terms of the dividend on the right side in descending order of their degree. Remember the sign! Also, if a term is missing, use $0$ as the coefficient. |\n| --- | ---: |\n| $3\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -5 & -7\\end{vmatrix}11; ↓; 2$ | Bring down the leading term of the dividend. Here, the leading term is ${\\color{red}2}$. |\n| $3\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -5 & -7\\end{vmatrix}11; 6; 2$ | Multiply the leading term $\\color{red}2$ by ${\\color{blue}3}$. This gives ${{\\color{blue}{3}}\\cdot \\color{red}{2}} = {\\color{green}6}$. Place the result below the next term. |\n| $3\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -5 & -7\\end{vmatrix}11; 6; 2 \\mid 1$ | Add the last result ($\\color{green}{6}$) to the term located above ($\\color{magenta}{-5}$) and write their sum below the line. This gives ${\\color{magenta}{-5}} + {\\color{green}{6}}={\\color{red}{1}}$. |\n| $3\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -5 & -7\\end{vmatrix}11; 6\\begin{vmatrix}3 \\\\ 2\\end{vmatrix}1$ | We now repeat the process. Multiply the last result ($\\color{red}1$ here) by $\\color{blue} 3$ and place the result below the next term. This gives ${\\color{blue}{3}}\\cdot {\\color{red}{1}}= {\\color{green}{3}}$. |\n| $3\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -5 & -7\\end{vmatrix}11; 6\\begin{vmatrix}3 \\\\ 2\\end{vmatrix}1 \\mid - 4$ | Now add the last result ($\\color{green}{3}$) to the term located above ($\\color{magenta}{-7}$) and write their sum below the line. This gives ${\\color{magenta}{-7}} + {\\color{green}{3}}={\\color{red}{-4}}$. |\n| $3\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -5 & -7\\end{vmatrix}11; 6\\begin{vmatrix}3 & -12 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}- 4 \\mid - 1$ | There is one last step. Again, multiply $\\color{blue} 3$ by the last result $\\color{red}-4$ and write it below the constant term. This gives ${\\color{blue}{3}}\\cdot{\\color{red}{(-4)}}={\\color{green}-12}$. Finally, add $\\color{green}-12$ to $\\color{magenta}11$ to get ${\\color{blue}{-1}}$, which is the remainder. The remainder $\\color{blue}-1$ is important, so we put a box around it. |\n\nThe numbers $2$, $1$ and $-4$ in the bottom row are the coefficients of the **quotient**. So from left to right, the quotient is\n\n$$\n2x^2+1x-4\n$$\n\nThe **remainder** is the value in the box, so ${\\color{blue}-1}$ in this case.\n\nFinally, we can write the full result of the division as\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2x^3-5x^2-7x+11}{x-3}=2x^2+x-4+\\dfrac{\\color{blue}-1}{x-3}\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies to\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2x^3-5x^2-7x+11}{x-3}=2x^2+x-4-\\dfrac{1}{x-3}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084439 #edb/ref 1065 3383 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084439 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "a99cb4a9-8428-584f-bcab-c2806d04719d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084439 #edb/ref 1067 "Dividing a Polynomial Using Synthetic Division" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084440 #edb/ref 1064 "We have already seen how synthetic division can be used to quickly divide a polynomial by a linear binomial with a leading coefficient of $1$.\n\nIn fact, synthetic division can be used when the divisor is *any* linear binomial, like $(ax+b)$. We just factor out the leading coefficient $a$, carry out the division in the standard way, and then include the leading coefficient in the final result.\n\nLet's see an example." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084440 #edb/ref 1065 3384 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084440 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "691913a1-b87e-59e2-b4f0-6a72bf964f18" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084440 #edb/ref 1067 "Dividing By a General Linear Factor" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084466 #edb/ref 1064 "Suppose that we want to divide two polynomials, such as\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2x^3-5x^2-7x+11}{x-3}\n$$\n\nFirst, let's get familiar with some terminology:\n\n- The **dividend** is the polynomial that we want to divide, so $2x^3-5x^2-7x+11$ in this case.\n- The **divisor** is the polynomial that we want to divide the dividend by, so $x-3$ in this case.\n- The result of the division, which will be a polynomial, is called the **quotient**.\n- The **remainder** is what is left after the division.\n\nBefore we start, we need to check that the polynomials are written in standard form. In our case, the terms in both the numerator and denominator are in descending order of their degree, so we're ready to go!" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084466 #edb/ref 1065 3928 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084466 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "0402dd10-0c81-5ad3-b813-6af9d4fe5fbc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084466 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084483 #edb/ref 1064 "Dividing $2x^3-5x^2-7x+11$ by $x-3$, we obtained that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2x^3-5x^2-7x+11}{x-3}=2x^2+x-4-\\dfrac{1}{x-3}\n$$\n\nNow, multiplying both sides by $x-3$, we get\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}2x^3-5x^2-7x+11}=(x-3)(2x^2+x-4)-1\n$$\n\nTherefore, to check if we have done the division correctly, we can simply multiply the polynomials on the right-hand side and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(x - 3)(2x^{2} + x - 4) - 1 &= x(2x^{2} + x - 4) - 3(2x^{2} + x - 4) - 1 \\\\\n&= 2x^{3} + x^{2} - 4x - 6x^{2} - 3x + 12 - 1 \\\\\n&= 2x^{3} - 5x^{2} - 7x + 11✓\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084483 #edb/ref 1065 4984 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084483 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "2e9f9179-dc6d-5214-a258-b8b1d6900457" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084483 #edb/ref 1067 "Checking the Division" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
